Short:        Today's pictures, sounds, films and documents for datatypes
Author:       AmiCradle Team
Uploader:     AmiCradle Team
Type:         util/dtype
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060
Distribution: MIT licence

GFOpenDatatypes is the AmiCradle Team's datatypes, in one pack, with an
Installer. Every program that opens files through datatypes (MultiView,
GFOpenBench, GFOpenBrowser, picture viewers, players) opens what they read.

On the Amiga itself:
  PNG pictures       gfopenpng.datatype, every colour type, with alpha
  Targa pictures     gfopentga.datatype
  WebP pictures      webp.datatype (libwebp)
  WebM films         webm.datatype (libvpx)
  CDXL films         cdxl.datatype
  Music modules      openmodule.datatype (libxmp): MOD, MED and OctaMED,
                     Oktalyzer, DigiBooster, XM, S3M, IT and more, through
                     AHI, else Paula

Through a services card or a paired Cradle (they ask gfopenservice.device's
media.decode/1 and doc.render/1; without one they say so and don't open):
  openpicture.datatype   AVIF, HEIC, JPEG XL, camera RAW, PSD, XCF, SVG...
  opensound.datatype     FLAC, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, AAC, ALAC, MP3, MIDI, SID
  openvideo.datatype     MP4, MKV, AVI, WMV, MPEG
  opendoc.datatype       DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, ODF, RTF, PostScript, EPUB...

And, ticked by default, the Team's datatypes.library 47.100 with the system
classes (picture, ilbm, sound, 8svx, text, ascii, animation, anim): API and
ABI compatible with AmigaOS 3.2's, written clean room.

Installing
----------
Open the GFOpenDatatypes drawer and double-click Install-GFOpenDatatypes. As a
Novice user everything goes in; as an Intermediate or Expert user you
choose each datatype, and whether the library and its classes go in.

Nothing is deleted: a file the pack replaces is kept in
SYS:Storage/GFOpenDatatypes/Superseded. Uninstall-GFOpenDatatypes, left in
SYS:Storage/GFOpenDatatypes, takes the pack out and puts those files back.
After installing or taking out the library, restart the Amiga.

Built for the 68040 with soft float, so a 68LC040 or 68EC040 is fine.
gzip.datatype, and gfopenpng.datatype's PNG writing, open z.library: the
pack brings the Team's own, GFOpenZlib (z.library 53.12), and installs it with
them; a z.library already there is kept and comes back with the uninstaller.
The datatypes that decode by a Cradle need gfopenservice.device (GFOpenUp's
GFOpenService part); the Installer says so when it is missing.

Source: https://github.com/DalsinAI/gfopendatatypes
